{"questions":[{"question_id":"oEYSqKy4Jhv50vE1","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2011","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"chemical-reactions-for-aldehydes-and-ketones","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"trichloroacetaldehyde-was-subjected-to-cannizzaros-reacti-2011-marks-4-oeysqky4jhv50ve1.htm","content":"Trichloroacetaldehyde was subjected to Cannizzaro’s reaction by using NaOH. The mixture of the\nproducts contains sodium trichloroacetate and another compound. The other compound is :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Trichloromethanol"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2, 2, 2-Trichloropropanol"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Chloroform"},{"identifier":"D","content":"2, 2, 2-Trichloroethanol "}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/rdNijLltRNRHYwJKH/qJeYX2Goko8qO4plmxZhm0eMELozk/EOkIufVWkIfi3x5TLPTUND/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2011 Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 271 English Explanation\"> \n<br>In Cannizzaro's reaction the compounds which do not contain <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-hydrogen atoms undergo oxidation and reduction simultaneously i.e. undergo disproportionation and form one molecule of sodium salt of carboxylic acid as oxidation product and one molecule of alcohol as reduction product. "}]}